{"step_index":48,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:32:54Z","input_tokens":3156,"cache_read_tokens":150245,"output_tokens":1160,"thinking":"Initial steering direction seems correct, confirmed across all frames. No issues detected in that area.\n\n\nAnalyzing steering behavior reveals a potential issue with the steering ratio. The initial ratio of 5.0 results in small steering wheel movements for significant steering angle changes. A more realistic ratio of 10.5 would provide appropriate steering wheel rotation for recorded scenarios.\n\n\nThe current approach avoids unnecessary mesh duplication by leveraging existing materials. Instead of adding fifteen material actions for the shift LEDs, three dedicated emission materials are introduced and driven by the RPM fraction within each gear. This ensures that the shift light bar on the steering wheel accurately climbs and resets on upshifts in the onboard scenarios. Additionally, this method allows for seamless replacement with a single `CLAY_Car` object in clay mode.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":8}}]}
