{"step_index":56,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:33:58Z","input_tokens":2755,"cache_read_tokens":155338,"output_tokens":3098,"thinking":"Initial check: Currently, `@env-2` is actively working on `v5_env.py`. Before `@env-2` finishes, verify all environment-track intersections. The `@verifier` hasn't posted results, so this double-check is necessary.\n\n\n`@env-2` is active, so any board updates will reach it immediately. Double-checking track clearance for `V5_HedgeRing` and `V5_Stand_Complex` with a short script is the priority, ensuring `@env-2` receives verified data. Also investigating camera occlusion fixes for `Cam_S04_Hairpin`, `Cam_S13_WoodcoteTele`, `Cam_S14_HeliDrop`, `Cam_S17_Maggotts`, and `Cam_S20_StoweTele` in the animation pipeline is next. Specifically, `Cam_S04_Hairpin` is blocked by `V5_Brake_1_150`; its position at `f=374..375` requires adjusting due to its current location behind the brake element along the curve's tangent.\n\n\nCamera `Cam_S04_Hairpin` adjustments result in no occlusions across the specified frames, with an improved view. For `Cam_S13_WoodcoteTele`, adjusting the `side` parameter to move the camera slightly inward resolves occlusion issues with the bridge pier and allows an unobstructed view.\n\n\nThe helicopter's perspective initially blocked the car's view under the bridge due to their relative positions at frame 1170. This was caused by the camera's line of sight passing through the bridge deck. Shifting the helicopter's starting position slightly ahead and higher resolves this issue and creates a visually compelling shot of the car emerging from under the bridge. Verifying the revised raycast confirms the improved view.\n\n\nRaising `Cam_S17_Maggotts`' height from 1.35m to 2.10m is necessary to resolve the occlusion by `V5_Barrier`. The initial camera height resulted in a line-of-sight that was below the barrier's height. The revised height ensures an unobstructed view throughout the specified frames. The new height is now 2.10.\n\n\nThe initial camera position placed the camera outside the track barrier, resulting in visual errors. The broadcast position of a telephoto camera at Silverstone Stowe was cross-referenced to determine the correct location. This location change ensured the camera was correctly positioned within the track's safety barriers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":8}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport bpy, json\nfrom mathutils import Vector\n\ndata = json.load(open(r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\track_data\\silverstone_track.json\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))\npts = [Vector((p[\"xy\"][0], p[\"xy\"][1], 0.0)) for p in data[\"points\"]]\ncx = sum(p.x for p in pts) / len(pts)\ncy = sum(p.y for p in pts) / len(pts)\nmax_r = max(((p.x - cx)**2 + (p.y - cy)**2)**0.5 for p in pts)\nprint(f\"Track center=({cx:.1f}, {cy:.1f}), max track radius from center={max_r:.1f} m\")\n\n# Check V5_HedgeRing min radius in current blend\nhr = bpy.data.objects.get(\"V5_HedgeRing\")\nif hr:\n    mw = hr.matrix_world\n    rs = [(((mw @ v.co).x - cx)**2 + ((mw @ v.co).y - cy)**2)**0.5 for v in hr.data.vertices]\n    print(f\"V5_HedgeRing radius range from track center: {min(rs):.1f} .. {max(rs):.1f} m\")\n\n# Check V5_Stand_Complex_Rail closest distance to track centerline\nsr = bpy.data.objects.get(\"V5_Stand_Complex_Rail\")\nif sr:\n    mw = sr.matrix_world\n    vs = [mw @ v.co for v in sr.data.vertices]\n    print(\"V5_Stand_Complex_Rail world verts:\", [(round(v.x,1), round(v.y,1), round(v.z,2)) for v in vs])\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\check_env_intrusion.py"}}]}
