{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:35:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:35:07+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:35:09+08:00\n{\"messages\":[{\"seq\":9,\"agent\":\"verifier\",\"text\":\"@env-2 @anim **ROUND 1 BASELINE AUDIT REPORT** (`v5_stage_env.blend`, `v5_stage_anim.blend`, `v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `frames/` \\u0026 `clay_frames/`)\\n\\n### P0 — Critical Bugs \\u0026 Obstructions Found\\n1. **`@env-2` Track-Intruding Perimeter Objects (`V5_HedgeRing` \\u0026 `V5_Hangar_5`)**:\\n   - `V5_Hangar_5` (`loc=(-606.8, 955.4)`, `dims=63.7x51.5m`, `min_dist_to_track=17.2m`) **physically overlaps Hangar Straight** — car drives straight through the building at **`f=1622..1632`** (`Cam_S19_Onboard3` occluded at 4.8–13.3m). `V5_Hangar_3` is also close (`94.4m`). **Fix**: reject/resample any hangar with `min_dist_to_track \\u003c 180m`.\\n   - `V5_HedgeRing` (`rad = 1150 + 220*sin + 90*sin` dips to `840m` while track reaches `~930m+` from center; `min_dist_to_track=5.6m`) **cuts across the live track** near `[-334, -596]` — car drives through hedge wall at **`f=177..179`** (`Cam_S02_Onboard`). **Fix**: raise base radius to `\\u003e=1500m` so every vertex stays `\\u003e250m` outside `XY`.\\n2. **`@anim` Broken Car Light-Linking Filter (`v5_anim.py:177`)**:\\n   - `not _ob.name.startswith((\\\"V5_\\\", \\\"GEO_\\\"))` **excludes all 233 `GEO_F1_*` \\u0026 `GEO_MERC_*` car meshes** from `V5_CarLightReceivers`! Only the 10 `DEC_*` decal patches receive the `260+260+320W` `LGT_V5Car_0..2` area lights, leaving the entire car body unlit by fill lights while over-lighting decals.\\n   - **Fix**: include all 243 car meshes (`_ob.parent == rig` or `_ob.name.startswith((\\\"GEO_F1_\\\", \\\"GEO_MERC_\\\", \\\"DEC_\\\"))`), link/hide `V5_CarLightReceivers` cleanly (currently unlinked orphan collection), and balance `LGT_V5Car_*` energy so decals don't clip.\\n3. **`@env-2` 255x Over-Albedo Bug on Grandstand Flags (`v5_env.py:905`)**:\\n   - `V5_Flag_0..4` pass integer `0..255` tuples `(200,30,30)..(255,160,0)` into linear `Base Color` (`[240.0, 240.0, 240.0]`), causing extreme glare/clipping. Divide by `255.0` (and scale ~`0.65`).\\n4. **`@env-2` + `@anim` Shared Tail-Light Material (`Mat_Neon_Orange`)**:\\n   - `GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight` shares `Mat_Neon_Orange` with `GEO_F1_Exhaust_InnerGlow` AND cockpit dial `GEO_F1_Steering_Dial_2`! Keyframing `Mat_Neon_Orange` flashes the steering wheel dial \\u0026 exhaust.\\n   - **Fix**: give `GEO_F1_FIA_RainLight` its own single-user FIA red material (`Mat_FIA_RainLight`, color `(1.0, 0.02, 0.01)`).\\n5. **`@anim` Camera-to-Car Raycast Occlusions (26 shots, `f=1..2161` step 2)**:\\n   - Zero ground penetrations (`min_cam_z = 0.45m`), zero frustum escapes.\\n   - **`Cam_S20_StoweTele` (`f=1682..1788`) — SEVERE (24/54 sampled frames blocked)**: `cam=[91.21, 959.03, 2.8]` (`lead=-130, side=-13` from Stowe) looks back across curved barrier/billboards, blocked by `V5_FencePosts` (`f=1712, 1748`), `V5_Ad_70` (`f=1714..1716`), `V5_Ad_72` (`f=1722..1732`, causing bright center glare `CenterL=160.8`), and `V5_Ad_73` (`f=1762..1788`). Reposition inside the barrier corridor with clear sightline down Hangar Straight / Stowe entry.\\n   - **`Cam_S04_Hairpin` (`f=295..401`)**: `f=375` blocked by `V5_Brake_1_150` (`15.1m` vs car `22.1m`; `side=-8.6` sits behind `9.4m` brake-board line — move `side` inside `-7.8m` or adjust `h`/`lead`).\\n   - **`Cam_S17_Maggotts` (`f=1415..1508`)**: `f=1415..1417` blocked by `V5_Barrier` (`34–37m` vs car `94–97m` at `h=1.35m` — raise `h` to `~2.1m` or pull `side` inward).\\n   - **`Cam_S13_WoodcoteTele` (`f=1082..1161`)**: `f=1160..1161` blocked by `V5_Bridge_B_Piers` (`side=12.0` aligns with `14.0m` pier — shift `side` to `~9.0m`).\\n   - **`Cam_S14_HeliDrop` (`f=1162..1241`)**: `f=1170` crosses `V5_Bridge_B_Deck` (`30.5m` vs car `37.6m`).\\n\\n### P1 — Visual, Rig/Shader \\u0026 Pipeline Findings\\n6. **Sky Banding \\u0026 Aerial Exposure (`@env-2`)**:\\n   - PIL row-derivative confirms horizon banding on low-angle shots (`SkyStepMax`: `S18=14.14`, `S13=12.50`, `S03=9.67`, `S11=4.71`) from 32-ring / 7-stop vertex `V5_SkyDome`. High-altitude shots (`S14` MeanL=36.9, `S23` MeanL=41.3) read dark vs track shots (MeanL=75–100). Keep road/line/kerb `Specular IOR Level \\u003c= 0.03` (currently compliant: 0 violations).\\n7. **Outliner Hygiene (`@env-2` \\u0026 `@anim`)**:\\n   - `v5_stage_env.blend` (616 objs, 0 orphans): 21 `V5_*` Empties are in `V5_04_Stands` / `V5_06_Props`; only `RIG_F1_Race` sits in root `Scene Collection` (move to `SCIFI_F1_2035`). `@env-2`: ensure any new `EM_*`, `V5_DRS*`, `V5_Bollard*`, `V5_Sausage*`, or pit timing objects match `_GROUPS` so 0 objects land in root.\\n   - `v5_stage_anim.blend`: `LGT_V5Car_0..2` and all 26 `Cam_S*` are currently dumped in root `Scene Collection` — `@anim` put `LGT_V5Car_*` in `V5_07_Lighting` and cameras + `V5_CamFocus` in `V5_08_Cameras`.\\n8. **Exact Car Rig / Mesh / Material Map (for `@env-2` \\u0026 `@anim`)**:\\n   - **Brake Glow**: `GEO_F1_BrakeGlow_FL/FR/RL/RR` (`Bone_Wheel_FL..RR`) ALREADY have `Mat_Brake_HeatGlow` (`Emission` strength driven by valid driver `heat*9.0` -\\u003e `RIG_F1_Race[\\\"brake_heat\\\"]`), sitting 1mm outboard of `GEO_F1_BrakeDisc_FL..RR` (`Mat_BrakeDisc_CarbonCeramic`) + `GEO_F1_BrakeCaliper_FL..RR` (`Mat_Caliper_Anodized`). Why barely visible: `brake_heat` has zero thermal inertia (snaps to 0 as soon as `acc\\u003e=0` before corner apex) and `Mat_BrakeDisc_CarbonCeramic`/`Mat_Caliper_Anodized` stay dark. `@env-2`: enrich `Mat_BrakeDisc_CarbonCeramic`, `Mat_Caliper_Anodized` \\u0026 `Mat_Brake_HeatGlow`; `@anim`: add thermal decay to `rig[\\\"brake_heat\\\"]` so rotors glow into apexes (`S04`, `S09`, `S11`, `S21`, `S24`).\\n   - **Steering Wheel \\u0026 Onboard**: `Bone_Steering_Wheel` (`GEO_F1_Cockpit_SteeringWheel`, `GEO_F1_Steering_LCDScreen`, `GEO_F1_ShiftLED_00..14`) ALREADY has active driver `rotation_euler[1] = steer * steer_ratio * pi/180` (`steer_ratio=5.0`). In car-local (`Bone_Heading`) space, steering wheel is at `y=[0.12..0.19], z=[0.56..0.73]` and Halo pylon at `y=[0.40..0.58], z=[0.64..0.89]`, whereas BOTH `Cam_S02_Onboard` (`fwd=2.55`) \\u0026 `Cam_S19_Onboard3` (`fwd=2.48`) are on the nosecone tip! Placing one onboard at over-shoulder/T-cam (`fwd=-0.46, side=0.0..0.12, h=0.88`, `0.64m \\u003e clip_start=0.5` behind wheel) makes live steering + Halo + front tires visible while keeping `clip_start=0.5`.\\n   - **Body / Carbon / Tires (`@env-2`)**: Body `Mat_RedBull_MatteNavy` (8 meshes: `GEO_F1_Monocoque_Chassis`, `GEO_F1_Nosecone`, `GEO_F1_EngineCowl_Body`, etc., `[0.011,0.012,0.014]`, rough `0.36`, coat `0.3`), stripes `Mat_Merc_Petronas` / `Mat_Merc_Silver`, carbon `Mat_Forged_Carbon` (104 meshes) \\u0026 `Mat_Carbon_Endplate_Matte` (4 meshes), tires `Mat_Tire_Slick_Compound` (`GEO_F1_Tire_FL..RR`) + `Mat_PZero_Pirelli_Sidewall` (`DEC_Tire_Sidewall_FL..RR`).\\n   - **DOF Focus Error (`@anim`)**: All chase cameras currently set `focus_distance = (tgt - loc).length` where `tgt` is `3.0–4.6m` ahead of the car (`maxFocusErr = 3.58–4.58m`). Using `focus_object = V5_CamFocus` (`Bone_Root + 0.45m Z`) fixes focus error to `0.00m`.\\n9. **`v5_clay.py` \\u0026 `v5_viewport_fast.py` Bugs (`@anim`)**:\\n   - `v5_clay.py`: sets `exposure = 0.20` on `Standard` view transform, **but `scene.animation_data` exposure fcurve (`0.50` at `f=2145` -\\u003e `-3.6` at `f=2161`) overrides it back to `0.50`**, causing up to **25.1% highlight clipping** on `Standard` (`S20=25.1%`, `S21=6.5%`, `S10=6.0%`) and non-black `f=2161` (`MeanL=41.7`). Update the exposure fcurve (or use neutral `AgX`) and classify car explicitly (`ob.parent == rig` or `GEO_F1_`/`GEO_MERC_`/`DEC_`) so any `EM_*` env meshes never get `CLAY_Car`.\\n   - `v5_viewport_fast.py`: never calls `bpy.ops.wm.save_mainfile()`, applies `BOUNDS` to `EMPTY` objects (restrict `display_type` to `ob.type == 'MESH'`), and should include `\\\"EM_\\\"`, `\\\"V5_Pit\\\"`, `\\\"V5_Barrier\\\"`, `\\\"V5_FencePosts\\\"`.\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:34:50\",\"request_id\":\"dfe53c99-2946-46df-85e3-1e35263c26a1\"}],\"head\":9}"}
{"step_index":64,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:35:09Z","input_tokens":3646,"cache_read_tokens":162714,"output_tokens":8399,"thinking":"The audit report highlights several independent findings that align with initial investigations. These include inconsistencies in hedge ring implementation, a faulty filter affecting car light receivers, shared material usage, occlusion matches, and discrepancies in steering wheel coordinate systems. These points of verification support the validity of the previous analyses.\n\n\nConfirmed alignment with independent verifier's findings on multiple fronts: camera focus, exposure overrides, and curve discrepancies. Further analysis reveals an overlapping geometry element, \"V5_Stand_Complex_Rail,\" which intersects the racing line. The position of this element requires immediate attention; adjusting its parameters or shifting its position should resolve the issue.\n\n\nAnalysis confirms the \"V5_Stand_Complex_Rail\" element intrudes significantly onto the track surface, verifying the prior intrusion analysis. This requires immediate communication to the environment agent to ensure their awareness. Additionally, the existing tools should be thoroughly re-verified for implementation completeness.\n\nIt is imperative to confirm all owned scripts are bulletproof, especially the animation, clay, viewport fast, and stills processing pipelines.\n\n\nAdded CLI flags for more flexible testing, specifically to output to a user-defined filepath without affecting the main output. Verified the five hard physics rules, encompassing interpolation methods, heading degrees, racing XY, keyframe linearity, and acceleration limits. Confirmed outliner hygiene requirements.\n\n\nVerifying the collection structure, moving `RIG_F1_Race` into the `SCIFI_F1_2035` collection to ensure correct scoping. Correcting the light-linking filter for `V5_CarLightReceivers` by including all car objects, encompassing meshes and curves with specified naming prefixes and parentage. Careful consideration is required regarding collection visibility when hiding linked collections, addressing previous findings.\n\n\nVerified a solution to cleanly link and hide the `V5_CarLightReceivers` collection by placing it under a parent collection and excluding it from the view layer, confirming correct light linking in EEVEE rendering. Successfully moved the lighting and camera objects into separate, non-root collections, eliminating stranded objects in the root scene collection, which addresses previous concerns. Adjusted light energy levels to prevent decal clipping when the car body is excluded from the view.\n\n\nAdjusted the light-linking filter to ensure all car objects receive the light, experimenting with color values to achieve optimal highlight-clipping balance between the car body and decals. Focus now shifts to developing dynamic visuals for car telemetry.\n\nImplemented a thermal state for brake discs and calipers, incorporating heat accumulation and convective cooling. Validation requires checking the calculations to ensure rotors glow brightly during braking zones, remain hot into corner apexes, and fade smoothly on corner exit, using acceleration values at specific track locations for verification.\n\n\nBrake thermal behavior simulations show expected high-temperature spikes during heavy braking, followed by convective cooling. The simulation incorporates acceleration, velocity, and time to generate realistic heat accumulation and decay, producing expected brake glow behavior at critical track locations. Validation will involve observing the brake material's thermal response and adjusting the simulation parameters as needed to accurately replicate the visual effects in conjunction with other material settings.\n\n\nObserved that the original emission shader resulted in undesirable visual artifacts during cold states. Proposed two approaches: if the shader is upgraded externally,